<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#zaju">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaju</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaju is a form of Chinese drama combining spoken dialogue, song and music, which reached its classical form under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>. Its four-act plays treated historical, romantic and moral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theme-system">themes</a>. The Yuan Dynasty profile notes that drama and narrative fiction flourished as Chinese literati, excluded from political careers, turned to these popular forms.</p></div>
